-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107, after review: a WITHIN that names a rule reading a
-- section GIVEN. Worked out in the module, it stopped with the evaluator's
-- "Internal error ... given signatures' values' lengths do not match. Please
-- report this as a bug."; it is not worked out now, and the reason says what
-- it reads.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`supplied` MEANS `the duty` WITH rate IS 4 PLUS 4

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`plain` MEANS `the duty`

§ `Terms`
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the window` MEANS rate TIMES 10

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`the duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `the window` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
